  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2018-10-10T10:07:56.682Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Now that crashers aren't as dangerous as they used to be, the majority of social conflicts involves players using voice chat to harass or annoy other people. Unfortunately, we can't record everything we want to report, especially since it's not as comfortable in VR as on desktop, but there may be a solution. \n\nI'm suggesting two options: \n\n1. Automatic system that records everything players say in voice chat (as well as all of their movements, emotes, use of emojis, hand gestures, at least potentially), stores only the most recent information, and sends the data regarding their activity over the past couple of minutes directly to the moderators as soon as the user in question gets reported.\n\n2. Ability to record video reports manually by using VRChat's virtual camera (in a special mode for capturing nameplates) without having to use any third-party software.\n\nEither way, most social platforms need tools accessible to users facing social conflicts, and VRChat is no exception.",
